  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Tom and Ben are at Sam's house. Sam has a small brown bear. \"Close your eyes,\" says Sam. Sam takes the bear to the garden. \"Open your eyes,\" he says. \"Find the bear!\" \"I say where to go.\" \"Do you understand?\" asks Sam. \"Yes!\" say Tom and Ben.",
      "\"Go to the tree,\" says Sam. Tom and Ben run to the tree. Pip runs too. \"Look under the box,\" says Sam. Ben looks under the box. There is a ball, but there is no bear. \"Open the door,\" says Sam. Tom opens the door. \"Look behind it!\" says Sam. There is a red shoe, but there is no bear.",
      "\"Where is the bear?\" asks Ben. \"Stand next to Pip,\" says Sam. Tom and Ben stand next to Pip. \"Now sit, Pip!\" says Sam. Pip sits down on the grass. He does not stand up. \"Pip, stand up!\" says Tom. Pip stands. The bear is under Pip! \"Woof!\" says Pip. The boys are happy."
    ],
    "summary": "Sam has a small toy bear. He gives Tom and Ben commands to find it, and Pip sits on the bear.",
